---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import FloatingBackControl from "../../components/common/FloatingBackControl.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Academic | Diego Carrillo"
  description="University education in robotics, automation and electronic engineering, complemented by professional studies in networking, cybersecurity, software practices and artificial intelligence."
>
  <section class="min-h-[calc(100svh-5rem)] bg-black px-6 py-10 sm:px-10 lg:px-16">
    <FloatingBackControl href="/#about" label="Back to about" />

    <article class="mx-auto mt-20 max-w-5xl pb-20">
      <p class="text-sm font-medium tracking-[0.22em] text-violet-300">ACADEMIC</p>
      <h1 class="interactive-heading mt-5 max-w-4xl text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-300 sm:text-6xl">
        Built on electronics, robotics and control.
      </h1>

      <section class="academic-section mt-16" aria-labelledby="university-education">
        <p class="section-label" id="university-education">ACADEMIC BACKGROUND</p>
        <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-base leading-8 text-slate-400">
          My academic background combines Electronic Engineering, postgraduate specialisation in Robotics and Automation, and networking studies, building a multidisciplinary foundation across intelligent systems, control and connected infrastructure. Completing studies in international environments allowed me to apply these concepts across different academic, technical and practical contexts.
        </p>

        <div class="learning-list academic-program-list mt-10">
          <article class="learning-item neon-box-panel">
            <h2>Master's Degree in Robotics and Automation</h2>
            <p>
              Postgraduate programme at Universidad Carlos III de Madrid focused on the design and development of robotic and automated systems, combining control, intelligent systems, software integration and experimental validation. The qualification includes the official European Diploma Supplement (SET).
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="learning-item neon-box-panel">
            <h2>Electronic Engineering</h2>
            <p>
              Engineering programme covering analogue and digital electronics, control, industrial automation, electrical machines, communications and data networks. Its practical component developed skills in analysing technical variables, designing solutions and integrating hardware with software.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="learning-item neon-box-panel">
            <h2>Cisco Systems CCNA</h2>
            <p>
              Networking programme focused on network fundamentals, switching, routing, IP connectivity and services, access control, security, automation and programmability. Its practical scope established a foundation for configuring, troubleshooting and protecting modern networked infrastructure.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="academic-section mt-20" aria-labelledby="professional-studies">
        <p class="section-label" id="professional-studies">ADDITIONAL STUDIES</p>
        <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-base leading-8 text-slate-400">
          These studies complement my background in AI, cybersecurity and software delivery.
        </p>

        <div class="learning-list mt-10">
          <article class="learning-item neon-box-panel">
            <h2>AI Neural Networks and Deep Learning</h2>
            <p>
              Foundational study of neural networks, deep learning architectures and their application to engineering guided by data and intelligent systems.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="learning-item neon-box-panel">
            <h2>Managing Network Security</h2>
            <p>
              Study of network threats, security controls and practices informed by risk for protecting connected systems and information flows.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="learning-item neon-box-panel">
            <h2>Software Processes and Agile Practices</h2>
            <p>
              Study of iterative delivery, collaborative development, planning and continuous improvement for reliable software products.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .academic-section {
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(196, 181, 253, 0.16);
    padding-top: 2.5rem;
  }

  .section-label {
    color: rgb(196 181 253);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
  }

  .learning-item p:last-child {
    color: rgb(148 163 184);
    line-height: 1.9;
  }

  .learning-list {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    max-width: 52rem;
  }

  .learning-item {
    padding: clamp(1.35rem, 3vw, 2rem);
  }

  .learning-item h2 {
    color: rgb(196 181 253);
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  .learning-item p:last-child {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 48.001rem) {
    .learning-item p:last-child {
      display: -webkit-box;
      overflow: hidden;
      -webkit-box-orient: vertical;
      -webkit-line-clamp: 2;
    }

    .academic-program-list .learning-item p:last-child {
      display: block;
      overflow: visible;
      -webkit-line-clamp: unset;
    }

    .academic-program-list .learning-item {
      min-height: 11.5rem;
    }
  }

</style>
